    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "cause": "Air in low-pressure circuit",
      "procedure": "Air may be in low-pressure circuit. Check it according to the following procedure. 1. Remove pressure pickup plug (outlet side) of fuel main filter. 2. Operate feed pump of fuel prefilter. 3. Check pressure pickup plug for leakage of fuel and air. If this error occurs during air bleeding after fuel filter is replaced, air may remain in fuel circuit. Keep running engine at low idle speed for approximately 3 minutes. As air is bled from fuel circuit, engine speed is stabilized, and error display disappears.",
